### ============================================================
### IMMUTABILITY GUARD SMOKE TEST
###
### Prerequisites:
###   - DEMO_MODE=true in apps/api/.env
###   - API running: pnpm dev (or pnpm --filter @sealed/api dev)
###   - Database seeded: pnpm db:seed
###
### How to use:
###   Click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom.
###   Each response opens in a side panel.
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001/api/v1
@authToken = demo

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 1: Verify auth works — get current user
### Expected: 200 OK with the seeded demo user
### ------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/me
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 2: List contacts
### Expected: 200 OK with at least one seeded contact
### ------------------------------------------------------------
# @name listContacts
GET {{baseUrl}}/contacts
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### Auto-extract the first contact's ID for use below:
@contactId = {{listContacts.response.body.data.0.id}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 3: Create a draft proposal
### Expected: 201 Created, status = "DRAFT"
### ------------------------------------------------------------
# @name createProposal
POST {{baseUrl}}/proposals
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "contactId": "{{contactId}}",
  "title": "Immutability Test Proposal",
  "description": "Testing that sent proposals cannot be edited",
  "lineItems": [
    {
      "description": "Consulting services",
      "quantity": 1,
      "unitPrice": 1000
    }
  ]
}

### Auto-extract the new proposal's ID:
@proposalId = {{createProposal.response.body.data.id}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 4: Update the DRAFT proposal
### Expected: 200 OK — DRAFT is mutable
### ------------------------------------------------------------
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated While Draft — This Should Work"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 5: Send the proposal (DRAFT → SENT)
### Expected: 200 OK, status = "SENT"
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 6: ⚠️ THE CRITICAL TEST
### Try to update the now-SENT proposal.
###
### Expected: 409 Conflict
### Body should contain:
### {
###   "code": "RESOURCE_IMMUTABLE",
###   "message": "Cannot modify proposal in status SENT. Only DRAFT is editable.",
###   "details": { "entityName": "proposal", "currentStatus": "SENT", "mutableStatuses": ["DRAFT"] }
### }
### ------------------------------------------------------------
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/proposals/{{proposalId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Sneaky Edit — This SHOULD FAIL"
}

### ============================================================
### BONUS: Verify agreement guard exists
###
### This creates a draft agreement, sends it, then tries to edit it.
### Expected: PATCH after /send returns 409 RESOURCE_IMMUTABLE.
### ============================================================

### ============================================================
### BONUS: Verify agreement immutability guard
### ============================================================

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 7: Create an agreement from our SENT proposal
###
### Note: There's no current status check on the proposal.
### This is a known gap we'll address separately.
### Expected: 201 Created (or 200 if HttpCode applied)
### ------------------------------------------------------------
# @name createAgreement
POST {{baseUrl}}/agreements
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "proposalId": "{{proposalId}}",
  "contactId": "{{contactId}}",
  "title": "Test Agreement",
  "body": "This is a test agreement body for immutability verification."
}

###
@agreementId = {{createAgreement.response.body.data.id}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 8: Update DRAFT agreement — should succeed
### Expected: 200 OK
### ------------------------------------------------------------
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/agreements/{{agreementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Updated Title While Draft"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 9: Send the agreement
### Expected: 200 OK, status = SENT
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/agreements/{{agreementId}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Step 10: Try to update SENT agreement — SHOULD FAIL
### Expected: 409 RESOURCE_IMMUTABLE
### ------------------------------------------------------------
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/agreements/{{agreementId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "This Should Be Blocked"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Verify normalized 404 shape
### Expected: { code: "RESOURCE_NOT_FOUND", message, timestamp, path, requestId }
### ------------------------------------------------------------
GET {{baseUrl}}/proposals/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}

### ------------------------------------------------------------
### Verify normalized validation error shape
### Expected: { code: "VALIDATION_ERROR", details: { errors: [...] }, ... }
### ------------------------------------------------------------
POST {{baseUrl}}/proposals
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "lineItems": []
}